{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact M6 head e5038a17d2ea85424ef33ccd65d490151eedd7bd on builder/typed-core-m6-20261107, tree 57648c38, all 25 artifact paths and the deletion of packages/derive/src/unsupported.ts, for request 0b0d2786 under promise c8c85693 and review request 75e3e9e3. Ordinary sends now run from instructions captured at admission, and each retained send routes its result to its own admitted occurrence. For every definition that parsed JSON can produce, the only behavior changes are the two fixes that my M5 and M4 approvals asked for.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- Scope. M5 main f04ff0f2 is an ancestor, the head is pushed, and the builder's worktree is clean at the head. Merge 654b8c77 joins main, and its tree equals its first parent's. The commit-message check passes: 8 checked, 0 flagged. The 26 paths are the derive source and tests, the generated Page module, three notes and eight manifests. No dependency, lockfile, gate script, seal, grant, wire type, platform source or Wrangler file changes. packages/derive/src/judge.ts does not change.\n- The gate. I read gate.exit at the gated source 71863e06, tree 0292a938: \"exit 0\". result.json records Node 135, Counting 56, Plain 4,016 with one skip and Native 1,111 with two skips, with no report error and no unhandled error. before.json and after.json are byte-equal: clean status, 4,193 tracked hashes, lockfile 5a717d43 and gate.sh 001c4b10, which equal the files at 71863e06. receipt.json records unchanged source and no owned process left. The mktemp wrapper only moves bare `mktemp -d` into the evidence directory. Between 71863e06 and this head, only three notes and the gate and Page CI manifests change, so docs/testing.md needs no new gate.\n- The Page module. GitHub reports run 42425270968 (Page browser scripts) as successful on the push of 71863e06. The asset freshness test ran inside the passing gate, and assets.ts has not changed since. Scope addendum 80bba3ac covers assets.ts.\n- The evidence. The eight manifests hash to the SHA-256 values that the note cites. Their 332 files match their sizes and digests and are read-only, and the credential scan finds no match. Each red fails by assertion on the old source. On M5 source 449979c2, the empty-name collect case, the two empty-list and two omitted-key observation-only cases, and the four mutation and alias result cases fail. The ownership case fails on the legacy executor. Pre-M5 main 3cb223b8 passes all four observation-only cases.\n- F1 from approval 80ef411d is fixed. validate/sends.ts captures an empty body for a row key that `result` omits, and runClause follows the occurrence's own result root. My M5 probe throws \"effects have no admitted body context\" on main f04ff0f2 and records `write` with no effects at the head, as pre-M5 main did. An independent probe matrix compares 32 full judgments: legacy and whole-scope cohorts, an empty or omitted list, `applied` or `refused`, and a right, stale, wrong or missing observation. The head equals pre-M5 main on all 32, and main throws on 8. The wrong observation still gives `authority-unavailable`.\n- The collect diagnostic from approval 3371681b is fixed. validate/sends.ts now tests `field !== false`. A definition with an empty field name stays refused, and its problem list again includes the collect's range and member problems. Across 175 validation cases, this is the only change in validator output.\n- The four M5 cleanups are done under addendum 8783d4ee. unsupported.ts is deleted and has no importer. The orphaned comment above readsUnbound is gone. `alsoRead` uses `conditionSubjects`, and its only use is an emptiness test. The package index now lists its effects and sends exports by name: they equal main's exports, minus `joinReturnedEffects` and the new `joinReturnedSends`.\n- The tests. No existing case or assertion changes. The only deleted test line is an import, replaced by one that names more symbols. The new cases compare complete results literally, in both capacity cohorts.\n- Semantics. An independent read of packages/derive/src against main, with probes on extracted trees, found these preserved:\n  - send encoding for every field type, presented-fact typing, `self`, `item`, `signer`, `scope`, `intent`, `none` and `const`. Party slots stay opaque;\n  - `if` on the before-entry view, and addresses, payloads and range predicates on the working view;\n  - the unbound-subject skip, omitted values, `n` ordinals, creation ordinals, causes, context, directory and membership;\n  - duplicate relations, collect and fan-out with `where`, `guard-incomplete` for an incomplete scan, and refusal details;\n  - the result-clause selection for every combination of the Native `always` counting rule, same-name conditional sends, fan-out reuse, a leading result and an empty list;\n  - reservation amounts. 517 admitted definitions give the same ok status, digest, `pendingWorkAmounts` and `reserving` in both trees;\n  - the Native returned-send validation block, which stays byte-identical behind `joinReturnedSends`.\n\nTwo more differences need a definition built in JavaScript, and both are fixes. Main and pre-M5 main both throw \"result clause was not captured by its validation\" when one send object appears twice in a list. The head runs each occurrence's own clause and reads each occurrence's own reservation key. Main also re-reads a declaration that something mutates after admission. The head keeps the admitted target, message, payload and result body. Parsed JSON produces neither case, and no production code mutates a declared definition.\n\nArchitecture: sound. Admission now owns every ordinary send: its code, its sources and its result body. Execution and result routing read those, not the declared forms. deriveSends and sendOrigin both check the body before they use it. Native marks stay behind one explicit bridge, so M7 can change their interiors without touching the written-send path.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The head changes no seal, grant, wire type, dependency or configuration, and judge.ts does not change. The validator records a captured plan only after the send's problem check passes, and the final structure pass runs only for an admitted definition, so an argument that the validator refuses never reaches a plan. Both join bridges are now internal to the package.\n\nSimplification: no required change. Four notes, for M7 or M8:\n\n1. A Native mark is still read live. deriveSends reads `always` from the raw mark (sends.ts line 188), and sendOrigin reads it from the admitted copy (send-origin.ts line 17). They agree unless something mutates the mark after admission. Read both from the admitted node when M7 moves the Native interiors.\n2. `formOf` (sends.ts line 296) is exported, and nothing in the repository calls it. It now returns null when two acts share one send list. Delete it or keep it out of the package index.\n3. In runClause, `clauses` now serves only the guard that tests for clauses without a captured body. That guard can test the captured body itself.\n4. sendOrigin calls `sendPlan` twice for each matched step, and the collect branch in `address` is unreachable.\n\nArchive request 64552d40 stays open. This approval closes no parent and no live acceptance, and authorizes no deployment.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:13ad539420b35c924d57b3d10d75b1f3093a03cd","binding":"assigned","head":"e5038a17d2ea85424ef33ccd65d490151eedd7bd","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:fdc6170f9e952e08e0ba13a3c3c24660b9af7d25\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:11fbfe048950032689e959830fe9e8a5efbf58ab\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c8c8569367016a10087a26e1b0801e5ea21e8c93\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8232842a1848bcce462a573462e99ca5903265e0","review_path":"reviewguard@